        "original_id": "24efb2f3-18aa-5768-980f-fa8133697552",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- People: Gordon Waller, Paul McCartney, Del Davis\n- Groups: Peter and Gordon, Lennon–McCartney\n- Songs: \"A World Without Love\", \"World Without Love\"\n- Albums: \"Mellow Dubmarine\"\n\nFacts:\n- Gordon Waller was born on 4 June 1945 and died on 17 July 2009.\n- Gordon Waller was a British singer-songwriter-guitarist.\n- Gordon Waller was best known as Gordon in the 1960s pop music duo Peter and Gordon.\n- Peter and Gordon's biggest hit was the No. 1 million-selling classic \"A World Without Love\".\n- Paul McCartney wrote \"A World Without Love\", and the song was attributed to Lennon-McCartney.\n- Del Davis recorded a cover of \"World Without Love\".\n- Del Davis's cover of \"World Without Love\" was featured on \"Mellow Dubmarine\".",
